menuconfig SPARKLINK
	bool "SparkLink (NearLink) subsystem support"
	depends on RUST
	depends on NET
	help
	  SparkLink (also known as NearLink / 星闪) is a short-range wireless
	  communication technology designed for low-latency, low-power, and
	  high-reliability scenarios including smart terminals, smart home,
	  smart vehicles, and industrial IoT.

	  This option enables the SparkLink protocol stack, providing:
	    - SCI (SparkLink Controller Interface) device management
	    - SLE (Synchronous Low Energy) air interface support
	    - Device discovery and service management
	    - Security management (SM2/SM3/SM4)

	  Say Y here to compile SparkLink support into the kernel or say M
	  to compile it as a module.

	  If unsure, say N.

if SPARKLINK

config SPARKLINK_SLE
	bool "SLE (Synchronous Low Energy) support"
	default y
	help
	  Enable support for the SparkLink SLE air interface, which provides
	  low-power wireless communication with synchronous scheduling.

	  This includes device discovery, connection management, and
	  data transfer over the SLE protocol.

config SPARKLINK_DEBUGFS
	bool "SparkLink debugging via debugfs"
	depends on DEBUG_FS
	default y
	help
	  Expose SparkLink subsystem debugging information through debugfs.

	  The debugfs entries will be created under /sys/kernel/debug/sparklink/.

source "drivers/sparklink/Kconfig"

endif # SPARKLINK
